## 1. UNDERSTAND THE ACTUAL PURPOSE

Guide is a personal tour-management application.

I receive booking inquiries from external platforms such as TourHQ, Viator, GetYourGuide, and potentially other tour-booking services. These platforms may send booking notifications and inquiries to my Gmail inbox.

My workflow is simple:

1. I open Guide and immediately see which dates are busy and which are available.
2. I open Orders and see genuine booking inquiries received through my email.
3. I inspect an inquiry and open the original email or the actual booking page on the platform.
4. I verify the inquiry and decide whether to accept it.
5. If I accept the booking, I do so directly on the external platform.
6. I return to Guide and manually record the confirmed booking or mark the relevant dates as busy.
7. I enter the dates, destination, reason, and any other useful information.
8. Guide saves the information and updates my calendar.

**Guide is my personal management tool. It must not pretend to accept bookings on external platforms automatically.**

I remain in control of accepting reservations and managing my availability.

Do not introduce unnecessary workflows, complicated dashboards, or features that do not support this process.

