## 11. ERROR HANDLING AND EDGE CASES

Handle common real-world situations properly:

- No booking inquiries found.
- Gmail access revoked.
- Gmail API rate limits.
- Network failures.
- Partial synchronization failures.
- Malformed email content.
- Missing client information.
- Unknown requested dates.
- Invalid date ranges.
- Multiple tours on the same day.
- Editing a tour's date.
- Deleting one of several tours on a date.
- Manually blocking a date that already contains a confirmed tour.
- Removing a manual block while a confirmed tour still exists.
- Double-clicking a button.
- Repeated synchronization.
- Expired authentication sessions.
- Firestore permission errors.
- Mobile viewport overflow.

Do not show a blank screen or silently fail when an error occurs.

Provide useful, human-readable feedback.

Ask for confirmation before destructive actions.

Disable actions while they are processing when appropriate.

